// naked-drums — an SFZ kit of k7-rack, a sampled acoustic one: Wilkinson Audio's Naked Drums, a 22" kick, five toms, two snares, hi-hat,
// ride, two crashes, splash and china, up to five velocity layers and ten round-robins, close mics and overheads
// mixed. CC BY 4.0, so it is credited here and in its description. Played by the engine's own SFZ player (sfizz),
// one ENGINE of k7-rack: a tap per piece, each its note through the whole kit.
//
// General MIDI notes: kick 36, side-stick 37, snare 38/40, toms 48 47 45 43 41, hi-hat 42 (closed) 44 (pedal)
// 46 (open), ride 51 (bell 53), crash 49 and 57, splash 55, china 52. The samples (~1.2 GB) are not in the library:
// the engine's machine keeps them, its supervisor fetching them once chosen in the tray's Downloads tab (k7-supervisor docs/instruments.md).
extends("@engine/sfz-player")
params({
  sfz: "@instruments/naked-drums/Wilkinson Audio/Naked Drums/User/Naked Drums GM.sfz",
  // Its loudest hit at full velocity, the snare, peaks at 0 dBFS — the level a rack's normalised samples play at.
  Volume: 2.1,
})
// The pads its panel draws, on the kit's General MIDI notes — the same names as the rack preset `Naked Drums`.
kit({
  Kick: 36,
  SideStick: 37,
  Snare: 38,
  Snare2: 40,
  Tom5: 41,
  HatTight: 42,
  Tom4: 43,
  HatPedal: 44,
  Tom3: 45,
  HatOpen: 46,
  Tom2: 47,
  Tom1: 48,
  Crash1: 49,
  RideBow: 51,
  China: 52,
  RideBell: 53,
  HatClosed: 54,
  Splash: 55,
  HatHalf: 56,
  Crash2: 57,
  Crash1Bell: 58,
  Crash2Bell: 59,
})
// A real acoustic drum kit, sampled close and from overhead with up to five velocity layers and ten round-robins per drum, on General MIDI notes — Naked Drums by Wilkinson Audio (CC BY 4.0). Its samples, about 1.2 GB, download from the k7 tray's Downloads tab.
